WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.740
Next morning, same tea stall.

2
00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.020
Meher and Arun, our made up

3
00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.700
friends, take up Article 44.

4
00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.060
One law for all on marriage,

5
00:00:10.060 --> 00:00:11.520
divorce, inheritance and

6
00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:12.430
adoption?

7
00:00:13.068 --> 00:00:15.428
The Constitution asks for it.

8
00:00:15.428 --> 00:00:17.248
Article 44:

9
00:00:17.248 --> 00:00:19.088
the State shall endeavour to

10
00:00:19.088 --> 00:00:21.538
secure a uniform civil code.

11
00:00:21.942 --> 00:00:24.022
It's a Directive Principle, so

12
00:00:24.022 --> 00:00:25.482
no court can enforce it.

13
00:00:25.482 --> 00:00:28.042
And Article 25 protects the

14
00:00:28.042 --> 00:00:29.932
freedom to practise religion.

15
00:00:30.433 --> 00:00:32.193
It's about equal rights.

16
00:00:32.193 --> 00:00:34.033
Today a woman's rights in

17
00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:35.813
marriage or inheritance can

18
00:00:35.813 --> 00:00:37.573
depend on her religion.

19
00:00:37.573 --> 00:00:40.183
One code treats all alike.

20
00:00:40.676 --> 00:00:42.436
Then fix the unfair rules.

21
00:00:42.436 --> 00:00:44.796
In 2018, the Law Commission

22
00:00:44.796 --> 00:00:46.536
said: reform within each

23
00:00:46.536 --> 00:00:47.736
personal law.

24
00:00:47.736 --> 00:00:48.856
Difference is not always

25
00:00:48.856 --> 00:00:49.786
discrimination.

26
00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:51.930
And it can work.

27
00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:54.330
Goa has long followed one civil

28
00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.030
code. In 1985, the Supreme Court

29
00:00:58.030 --> 00:00:59.470
said it would help national

30
00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:00.500
integration.

31
00:01:01.222 --> 00:01:02.722
But customs differ.

32
00:01:02.722 --> 00:01:04.802
Even Uttarakhand's and Gujarat's

33
00:01:04.802 --> 00:01:06.382
new codes leave out Scheduled

34
00:01:06.382 --> 00:01:07.902
Tribes, whose customs the

35
00:01:07.902 --> 00:01:09.972
Constitution itself protects.

36
00:01:10.438 --> 00:01:12.238
What the record says.

37
00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:14.858
Article 44 is a directive.

38
00:01:14.858 --> 00:01:17.118
In 2018, the Law Commission

39
00:01:17.118 --> 00:01:18.918
called a uniform code neither

40
00:01:18.918 --> 00:01:21.618
necessary nor desirable then.

41
00:01:21.618 --> 00:01:24.718
Uttarakhand passed one in 2024,

42
00:01:24.718 --> 00:01:26.888
Gujarat in 2026.

43
00:01:28.218 --> 00:01:29.578
For GS2 and GS1:

44
00:01:29.578 --> 00:01:31.218
both sides, fairly.

45
00:01:31.218 --> 00:01:34.788
Then a balanced way forward.

46
00:01:35.741 --> 00:01:37.921
Their order was the one uniform

47
00:01:37.921 --> 00:01:41.621
thing: two glasses, same tea.

48
00:01:41.621 --> 00:01:44.291
The question stays on the table.
